      "subset": "S5",
      "task_type": "cross-company-year-hybrid",
      "question": "Calculate the percentage increase in NFLX's total revenues from FY2022 to FY2024 and the percentage increase in paid memberships over the same period. How do these growth rates compare, and what does META's FY2022 and FY2024 MD&A provide for user or revenue metrics?",
      "expected_answer": "NFLX total revenues grew from $31,615,550 thousand in FY2022 to $39,000,966 thousand in FY2024, a 23.4% increase ($39,000,966 - $31,615,550) / $31,615,550 * 100 = 23.35%). Paid memberships at end of period grew from 230,747 thousand to 301,626 thousand, a 30.7% increase (($301,626 - $230,747) / $230,747 * 100 = 30.73%). Revenue grew slower than membership base, indicating ARPU pressure or mix shift. META's Item 7 for both FY2022 and FY2024 provides only introductory text with forward-looking statements, no revenue or user metrics, so no comparable data exists in the provided documents.",
      "predicted_answer": "**NFLX FY2022→FY2024 percentage increases:** Paid memberships rose 693.3% [C1], based on 38,023 thousand at FY2022 end [F2][E4] versus 301,626 thousand at FY2024 end [F3][E5].\n\n**NFLX total revenues:** FY2024 total revenues of $39,000,966 thousand and FY2022 total revenues of $3,570,221 thousand are both retrieved [F1][E4][E5], but no revenue growth percentage is provided in the verified calculations, so the FY2022→FY2024 revenue percentage increase cannot be computed from the supplied ledger.\n\n**META:** FY2022 annual worldwide ARPP was $31.79, down 6% from 2021 [E1]; FY2024 annual worldwide ARPP was $49.63, up 15% from 2023 [E2]. META also reported worldwide DAP increased 5% to 3.35 billion in December 2024 from 3.19 billion in December 2023 [E2].\n\nSources:\n[E4] NFLX_2022.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E5] NFLX_2024.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E1] META_2022.html — Item 7, MD&A\n[E2] META_2024.html — Item 7, MD&A",
